      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "638ff54a7369f037dd6fcead",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I was following some posts about optimizing animation controllers, and I came across some rather fun information. Turns out, if the Animation Controller has a LOT of Layers, the avatar will perform poorly. Yet, I wanted to have a lot of features/toggles on my avatar, and each \"toggle\" was its own separate Layer. I actually ended up optimizing my Layer count from 32 Layers to 16 by combining a bunch of them into one single Direct Blend Tree Layer.\n\nhttps://notes.sleightly.dev/dbt-combining/\n\nThis guide fixed my frame drop issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-07T02:07:06.312Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For some reason the more animations there is overall in the avatar descriptor, the more the framerate drop in station. Humanoid/ blend tree seen to have a the biggest impact since they have usually more property and frames.\n\nThe easiest way to reproduce it is to duplicate a walking blend tree like 50-100 times for good measures.\n\nWhy only in station, that I don't know.",
